# RespawnPack — CODEOWNERS  (installed to .github/CODEOWNERS)
#
# WHY: sensitive paths get a mandatory review gate. With "Require review from Code
# Owners" enabled in branch protection, GitHub blocks a merge to these paths until a
# listed owner approves. This is the persistent complement to the in-session `lockdown`
# hook — lockdown scopes edits while you work; CODEOWNERS gates them at merge time, for
# every contributor, even outside Claude.
#
# Fill in real owners (@user or @org/team) before relying on it. Until you do, these
# lines reference a placeholder team and will not enforce. Adjust the paths to your repo.

# Default owner for everything (replace with your team):
*                    @your-team

# Sensitive paths — require explicit owner review (the same surfaces /ship gates on):
/auth/               @your-team
/payments/           @your-team
/billing/            @your-team
**/migrations/       @your-team
/infra/              @your-team
/.github/            @your-team
/.claude/            @your-team
